Thanks @nvpohanh. I added a **Reproduction** section to the description:
- the hardware (8× B300) and the image digest;
- the full server launch command, including `--hicache-size` and the EAGLE flags, and what changes for each other arm;
- the InferenceX AgentX benchmark command and trace source;
- how the synthetic acceptance length is fixed;
- the GSM8K command with the `--max-total-tokens 131072` cap.

The docs row and a TP2 end-to-end test are in cf4301d11e (replies inline).

[by Claude Code] **Severity: style | Confidence: High**

**Issue**

The Accuracy and Performance sections give results and describe the setup in prose, but someone else cannot rerun them. The description does not include:
- the GPU type (it says only "one 8-GPU node");
- the full server launch commands for the control and dedup arms, including the `--hicache-size`/`--hicache-ratio` values and the EAGLE flags;
- the benchmark command, the source of the agentic-coding trace, and how the fixed synthetic acceptance length was set;
- the GSM8K command, and the flag that capped the device KV pool at 131,072 tokens.

**Fix**

Please add these commands and the GPU type to the description.

